The themes, icons, cursors and terminal color scheme in these directories
come from Chicago95 by grassmunk and its contributors:

  /usr/share/themes/Chicago95
  /usr/share/icons/Chicago95
  /usr/share/icons/Chicago95_Animated_Hourglass_Cursors
  /usr/share/icons/Chicago95_Standard_Cursors
  /usr/share/xfce4/terminal/colorschemes/Chicago95.theme

Upstream: https://github.com/grassmunk/Chicago95
License, as upstream gives it in README.md: GPL-3.0+/MIT. GPL-3.0.txt is the
text of the GNU General Public License, version 3. CREDITS is the file of
the upstream source tree.

Source and changes: elements/winblues/chicago95.bst in
https://github.com/tuna-os/brussels gives the upstream commit and the
commands that remove files from the upstream tree and replace the start menu
icon. The project builds the files from that commit and does not edit them.

The start menu icon is Tux by Larry Ewing (lewing@isc.tamu.edu), made with
The GIMP. The pixel version comes from Chicago95.
